Implemented all required artifacts:

- [solution.py](/work/solution.py) and generated [solution.mpy](/work/solution.mpy)
- [semantic.k](/work/semantic.k): custom executable semantics
- [verification.k](/work/verification.k) and [spec.k](/work/spec.k): symbolic contract, inductive invariant, examples, and boundary claims
- [prove.sh](/work/prove.sh): complete reproducible command sequence

Validation:

- Both prompt examples passed under `krun`.
- 2,000 randomized CPython oracle checks passed.
- All three proof stages printed `#Top` and exited 0. The loop lemma is proved independently before being reused in the symbolic end-to-end proof.

RESULT: KPROVE_PASSED — Every positive kprove command in prove.sh printed #Top and exited 0.
diff --git a/prove.sh b/prove.sh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a75902d756a5155eec07e719477b88c066b285a1
